+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+Measured with `muninn-bench`'s adversarial synthetic vocabulary: a Zipf-distributed
+corpus of 30 frequent domain words plus ~2,000 rare identifiers, built to make
+posting lists look like real code discussion instead of a corpus where every
+record contains every term (`crates/muninn-bench/src/main.rs`, `WORDS` / `word()`).
+
+- **Before the term-selection fix:** full `UserPromptSubmit` hook p95 was
+  **10.27 ms** on this adversarial 30-word vocabulary.
+- **The fix:** in IDF-based term selection (`crates/muninn-core/src/recall.rs`,
+  `select_terms`), drop candidate terms whose document frequency `df` exceeds
+  `n/3` (for stores with `n >= 50` records) — a term appearing in more than a
+  third of the store carries no IDF signal but still costs a long FTS5 posting
+  list scan.
+- **After the fix:** full `UserPromptSubmit` hook p95 dropped to **1.82 ms**
+  on the same adversarial vocabulary.
+
+Provenance note: these two numbers come from this project's own prior
+measurement runs (a trust-1 `muninn` memory episode reporting the perf
+comparison), not from a checked-in benchmark report in this repository. A
+repo-local search (`crates/muninn-bench`, `research/00-evidence-log.md`,
+`research/CONCLUSION*.md`) found no file that records the literal 10.27 ms /
+1.82 ms figures; only the `df > n/3` guard the fix describes was found
+committed in `recall.rs`. Re-run `muninn-bench perf` (see the "hook
+UserPromptSubmit full p95" contract in `crates/muninn-bench/src/main.rs`) to
+reproduce or refresh these numbers if a committed record is needed.
